* TRAK      174 11081    ERROR DETECTION SUBROUTINE                     TRAK0001
*     FAP                                                               TRAK0002
NUTRAK COUNT 200                                                        TRAK0003
*NUTRAK STANDARD ERROR TRACER. 7090 VERSION OF J. COOLEY,S NUBACK FOR704TRAK0004
*      REWRITTEN FOR THE 7090 BY F. RAGUSA. AUGUST 1961.                TRAK0005
* TO USE WITHIN A FORTRAN PROGRAMCALL NUTRAK (I,N,BCD,C,D,.....,Y,Z)    TRAK0006
* TO USE WITHIN A FAP PROGRAM CALL NUTRAK ,I,N,LBCD,C,D,....,Y,Z        TRAK0007
*    WHERE     I=0  IF ONE WANTS TO SIGNAL THAT TRAK  HAS BEEN CALLED   TRAK0008
*               BY PRINTING THE CURRENT VALUE OF C AND D.               TRAK0009
*      OR      I=SOME NUMBER OTHER THAN ZERO IF ONE WANTS TO PERFORM THETRAK0010
*               ENTIRE BACK TRACE FROM THE CALLING PROG. TO THE MAIN    TRAK0011
*      AND     N=0  CAUSES PRINTING ON LINE  (IF NOT IN MONITOR MODE)   TRAK0012
*      OR      N= NUMBER OF THE TAPE ON WHICH OUTPUT IS TO BE WRITTEN   TRAK0013
*      NOTE    IF IN MONITOR MODE (SENSE SWITCH 6 UP) N IS ALWAYS       TRAK0014
*              ASSUMED TO BE EQUAL TO 6 (A3) THE MONITOR,S OUTPUT TAPE. TRAK0015
*      AND     BCD = TO A HOLLERITH ARGUMENT OF NOT MORE THAN 120 BCD   TRAK0016
*              CHARACTERS.  THESE CHARACTERS WILL BE PRINTED AS THE     TRAK0017
*              FIRST LINE OF OUTPUT UPON ENTRY TO TRACK.                TRAK0018
* FAP NOTE     BCD= LOCATION OF WHERE HOLLERITH CHARACTERS HAVE BEEN    TRAK0019
*              STORED IN MEMORY (FORWARDS).                             TRAK0020
*FORTRAN NOTE  BCD= TO AN ARGUMENT OF THE FORM.. 72H PRINT THIS ETC.,   TRAK0021
*      AND     C,D,E,....Y,Z   ARELOCATIONS OF NUMBERS ONE WANTS PRINTEDTRAK0022
*      NOTE    THERE MAY BE ANY NUMBER OF SUCH QUANTITIES, OR NONE.     TRAK0023
*                       AND AWAY WE GO                                  TRAK0024
       ENTRY   NUTRAK                                                   TRAK0025
NUTRAK SXD     *-2,4                                                    TRAK0026
       CAL     LHOL           A TSX HOLLY,0,0                           TRAK0027
       SLW     COULD+1                                                  TRAK0028
       CLA     1,4     IF I IS NOT ZERO THEN IT MUST BE SOME NUMBER LESSTRAK0029
       STA     ONCE     THAN 100 OR THE ARGUMENT  IS ASSUMED TO BE THE  TRAK0030
       ANA     =O77777    ADDRESS OF WHERE I IS LOCATED.                TRAK0031
       CAS     =O143                                                    TRAK0032
       TRA     ONCE                                                     TRAK0033
 STORY NOP                                                              TRAK0034
       ALS     18                                                       TRAK0035
       TRA     UPON                                                     TRAK0036
 ONCE  CLA     **                                                       TRAK0037
 UPON  STD     I                                                        TRAK0038
       SWT     6       S.S. 6 TESTS FOR MONITOR MODE.                   TRAK0039
       TRA     ATIME   UP= IN MONITOR MODE                              TRAK0040
       CLA     2,4     DOWN= OUTSIDE MONITOR                            TRAK0041
       ANA     =O777777                                                 TRAK0042
       CAS     =O144   IF ADDRESS  GREATER 144 THEN=L(TAPE NO.) WORD    TRAK0043
       TRA     THERE                                                    TRAK0044
       TRA     THERE    DITTO IF EQUAL TO 144                           TRAK0045
       ALS     18      IF LESS THAN 144 THEN ADDRESS IS THE TAPE NUMBER TRAK0046
       TRA     WAS                                                      TRAK0047
 ATIME CLA     SIXDC   WHEN IN MONITOR MAKE TAPE = A3 (6)               TRAK0048
       TRA     WAS     FOR OUTPUT . IGNORE ARGUMENT OF ZERO FOR ONLINE  TRAK0049
 THERE CLA*    2,4                                                      TRAK0050
 WAS   STD     TAPNO                                                    TRAK0051
       CLA     TAPNO   IF TAPE NO. (N)= 0 AND RUN IS OUTSIDE MONITOR USETRAK0052
       TZE     AHEP    FORTRAN ROUTINE SPH  INSTEAD OF  STH.            TRAK0053
       CAL     CALTN    THIS IS A  CAL TAPNO USED FOR STH ROUTINE       TRAK0054
       SLW     REALY    PARDON THE SPELLLING                            TRAK0055
       SLW     THIS                                                     TRAK0056
       CAL     A(STH)    A TSX  $(STH),4                                TRAK0057
       TRA     CAT                                                      TRAK0058
 AHEP  CLA     STORY    A  NOP                                          TRAK0059
       STO     REALY                                                    TRAK0060
       STO     THIS                                                     TRAK0061
       CAL     A(SPH)   A  TSX $(SPH),4                                 TRAK0062
 CAT   SLW     COULD                                                    TRAK0063
       SLW     DAD                                                      TRAK0064
       CLA     NUTRAK-1                                                 TRAK0065
       STO     NAME                                                     TRAK0066
       STZ     IFN  INTERNAL FORMULA NUMBER                             TRAK0067
       STZ     EFN     EXTERN                                           TRAK0068
       CLA     3,4    LOCATION OF HEADING  IN BCD                       TRAK0069
       STA     HEDING                                                   TRAK0070
       SXA     X2,2                                                     TRAK0071
       SXA     X1,1                                                     TRAK0072
       AXT     0,2                                                      TRAK0073
       AXT     12,1                                                     TRAK0074
HEDING CAL     **,2                                                     TRAK0075
       LAS     =O777777777777   IS THE BCD WORD THE FENCE               TRAK0076
       TRA     *+2     NO                                               TRAK0077
       TRA     FENCE     YES                                            TRAK0078
       SLW     HOLLY+14,1     STORE THE BCD WORD IN OUR BUFFER          TRAK0079
       TXI     *+1,2,-1    PICK UP NEXT WORD (STORED FOWRWARDS)         TRAK0080
       TIX     HEDING,1,1   STORE MAXIMUM OF 12 WORDS ONLY              TRAK0081
       TRA     X2                                                       TRAK0082
 FENCE CAL     =H        IF LESS THAN 12 BCD WORDS FILL BUFFER WITH BLKSTRAK0083
       SLW     HOLLY+14,1                                               TRAK0084
       TIX     *-1,1,1                                                  TRAK0085
 X2    AXT     **,2                                                     TRAK0086
 X1    AXT     **,1                                                     TRAK0087
       TXI     *+1,4,-3                                                 TRAK0088
 WHAT  SXA     SWING,4                                                  TRAK0089
 REALY PZE     0       THIS WILL BE A NOP OR A CAL TAPNO                TRAK0090
 COULD TSX     **,4    THIS WILL BE TO SPH OR STH                       TRAK0091
       TSX     HOLLY,0,0  LOCATION OF FORMAT STORED FORWARDS            TRAK0092
       LDQ     EFN                                                      TRAK0093
       STR             PART OF FORTRAN OUTPUT RTN. CALLING SEQUENCE     TRAK0094
       LDQ     IFN                                                      TRAK0095
       STR                                                              TRAK0096
       TSX     $(FIL),4                                                 TRAK0097
       CAL     LF1                                                      TRAK0098
       SLW     COULD+1          A TSX F1,0,0                            TRAK0099
 SWING AXT     **,4    SEE SYM. LOC. WHAT  WHICH STORES ADDRESS HERE    TRAK0100
       TXH     SWEET,4,0                                                TRAK0101
 NOW   LXD     NUTRAK-2,4                                               TRAK0102
       CAL     4,4                                                      TRAK0103
       ANA     =O700000000000                                           TRAK0104
       TNZ     4,4                                                      TRAK0105
       TXI     NOW+1,4,-1                                               TRAK0106
SWEET  SXD     IR,4                                                     TRAK0107
 WHEN  CAL     1,4                                                      TRAK0108
       ANA     =O700000000000                                           TRAK0109
       TNZ     PAD                                                      TRAK0110
       CLA     1,4                                                      TRAK0111
       STA     TOOK                                                     TRAK0112
       STA     HIS                                                      TRAK0113
       STA     HORN                                                     TRAK0114
       SXA     TOA,4                                                    TRAK0115
 THIS  PZE     0       THIS IS A NOP OR A CAL TAPNO                     TRAK0116
 DAD   TSX     **,4    THIS IS TO STH OR SPH                            TRAK0117
       TSX     F2,0,0  F2 IS THE FORMAT AND THE TSX USED BECAUSE ITS FORTRAK0118
 TOOK  LDQ     **    ARGUMENT WILL BE FIRST A AND THEN B         WARD   TRAK0119
       STR                                                              TRAK0120
 HIS   LDQ     **                                                       TRAK0121
       STR                                                              TRAK0122
 HORN  LDQ     **                                                       TRAK0123
       STR                                                              TRAK0124
       TSX     $(FIL),4                                                 TRAK0125
 TOA   AXT     **,4                                                     TRAK0126
       TXI     WHEN,4,-1                                                TRAK0127
 PAD   CLA     I                                                        TRAK0128
       TZE     NOW                                                      TRAK0129
       CLA     1,4                                                      TRAK0130
       STD     EFN                                                      TRAK0131
       CLA     2,4                                                      TRAK0132
       STD     IFN                                                      TRAK0133
       STA     THE+1                                                    TRAK0134
       ANA     =O77777                                                  TRAK0135
       TZE     JOINT                                                    TRAK0136
       CAS     =O77777                                                  TRAK0137
       TRA     *+2                                                      TRAK0138
       TRA     WOULD                                                    TRAK0139
       ADD     =1                                                       TRAK0140
       STA     THE                                                      TRAK0141
 THE   CLA     **                                                       TRAK0142
       LXD     **,4                                                     TRAK0143
       STO     NAME                                                     TRAK0144
       TRA     WHAT                                                     TRAK0145
 JOINT CLA     MAIN                                                     TRAK0146
       AXT     0,4                                                      TRAK0147
       TRA     THE+2                                                    TRAK0148
 WOULD LXD     IR,4                                                     TRAK0149
       CLA     -1,4                                                     TRAK0150
       STA     THE+1                                                    TRAK0151
       CLA     MAIN+1                                                   TRAK0152
 ROCK  TRA     THE+1                                                    TRAK0153
*                                                                       TRAK0154
 MAIN  BCI     1,MAIN-                                                  TRAK0155
       BCI     1,FU-DEF                                                 TRAK0156
 HOLLY BCI 1,(1H4,                 SHOULD GIVE DOUBLE SPACE BEFORE ENTRYTRAK0157
       BCI 1,75H                                                        TRAK0158
       BSS     12                                                       TRAK0159
 F1    BCI     1,/14H0                                                  TRAK0160
 NAME  BCI     7,        EFN=I5,7H   IFN=I5,11H   ARG.ARE-)             TRAK0161
 F2    BCI ,(11H0     OCT  O12,10H     DEC  1PE14.7,10H     INT  I15)   TRAK0162
 I     PZE     0                                                        TRAK0163
 SIXDC PZE     0,0,6                                                    TRAK0164
 TAPNO PZE     0                                                        TRAK0165
 CALTN CAL     TAPNO                                                    TRAK0166
A(STH) TSX     $(STH),4                                                 TRAK0167
A(SPH) TSX     $(SPH),4                                                 TRAK0168
 IFN   PZE     0                                                        TRAK0169
 EFN   PZE     0                                                        TRAK0170
 IR    PZE     0                                                        TRAK0171
 LHOL  TSX     HOLLY,0,0                                                TRAK0172
 LF1   TSX     F1,0,0                                                   TRAK0173
 THEND END                                                              TRAK0174
